00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.550
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.320
MISRA: Thank you.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.940
When Anne called me
several months ago

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:10.560
to create a lecture for this
series, I kind of initially

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:16.310
thought that I will
talk with cognition.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:24.530
Cognition as a topic has
interested me strongly,

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:36.890
because more and more as I grow
older, I believe that we become

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.290
prey to perception.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:44.490
Perception in a sense of
electrical engineering,

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.070
that is, where is the signal?

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:49.690
What is the signal?

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.550
Do we have a signal?

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.620
Can we get the signal?

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:59.110
How much of error is there in
our sights, in our hearing,

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:05.770
in our feeling, in our
overall sensory reception?

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:10.300
How did I come to feel
about this strongly

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:18.380
is different people, scientists,
various enlightened people,

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.250
various people with
a lot of information,

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:26.280
will present information
somewhat differently.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:32.250
That is how I felt that we
must have a good understanding

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.510
of perception.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:37.320
However, when I wanted
to prepare the talk

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.272
and then I talked to her
again when she spoke me back,

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:41.730
I said, well-- she
said that, look,

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.650
you must speak from
the Hindu perspective.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.840
I said, well, if
Hindu perspective,

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:50.440
I will talk about my
favorite philosopher.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:53.650
So what you will
hear from me today

00:05:53.650 --> 00:06:00.460
is about someone I admire
strongly who lived in India

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:05.050
and whose work I think
has a great importance

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:11.110
in the present-day understanding
of cognition and intelligence.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:13.200
His name is Shankara.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.205
What I will guide
you through is--

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:42.140
Since it's supposed to be Hindu
talk, so I will kind of first

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:43.910
give you a little
bit of background

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:46.650
about what Hindus think.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:50.880
And then I will put Shankara
in the Hindu manifold.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.587
The Hindus' ideas
are the following--

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:04.180
Hindu as the word
probably is not very old,

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.700
but Indian as a word
probably is more older.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.940
Indian means, like-- India
was called differently before,

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:13.600
but things coming from India.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.050
So a long time ago, I would
say several thousand years ago,

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:21.100
definitely there was a
time where Indians strongly

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:25.290
felt about finding
something called truth.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.730
Now, truth in this
particular point of view,

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.530
or a mathematical
point of view--

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.920
if you read the scriptures
and literature strongly,

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.460
you will find what was bothering
them was something that

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.880
has little higher time scale.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.890
Something is not transient.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.890
Something will leave tomorrow.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:47.660
And tomorrow may be
somewhat like 100 years,

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.100
500 years, 1,000 years,
depending upon the philosopher.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.320
This particular
thing, which we'll

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:57.820
call being, which
says something exists.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.750
All right?

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.650
That will be called truth.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.880
Something is being.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.360
Now, from that
being, [INAUDIBLE]

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:11.280
create a situational
philosophy of this being,

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.380
so basically you have
being and non-being.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:20.310
And from the beings, things
that are somewhat permanent,

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:23.580
somewhat in the world,
in some stability,

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:26.400
they will create the philosophy,
the fundamental parts

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:31.630
of which philosophy would
be consciousness and nature.

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:38.200
That is, all beings are endowed
with two fundamental qualities,

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.010
consciousness and nature.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:44.350
These are Sanskrit words
which have translated,

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:47.770
but basically they're kind
of close literal translation.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:50.650
Nature is the property of
the individual, the property

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:53.710
of the being, the way
the being operates,

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:56.080
the way the being
interacts with society,

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.990
the way the being interacts
with the environment.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:05.620
Consciousness is something
that helps him, helps her,

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.855
helps it do things.

00:09:07.855 --> 00:09:09.900
All right?

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:17.910
So this separation, which has
no metaphysical or godly impetus

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:23.020
in it, was very basic,
that everybody's

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:27.010
endowed with a consciousness
and with a nature.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:30.480
And nature can be
of diverse manifold,

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:34.440
but consciousness is
a part of the being

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:38.320
in order to activate the nature.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:41.040
Going somewhat
further, the nature

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.315
would have three
different elements.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:55.530
Nature's manifestation is
the body, the physical body.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:59.170
That body will have
three different elements.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:06.190
The first element, intellect,
intelligence, and ego.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:12.720
Intellect is something that
you are endowed with, genetic.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:18.810
Intellect is something
that you have less control,

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:23.220
but somehow which
helps you organize,

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:32.680
which helps you obtain things
and accommodate things.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.710
Intelligence is
something that you

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:40.880
do, your cognitive abilities,
your brain activities,

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:43.430
in which you try to manipulate.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.320
You try to obtain.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.670
You try to create.

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:48.530
You try to accommodate.

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:51.930
Or as [INAUDIBLE] says,
you try to assimilate.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:55.210
Those are all true
for intelligence.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.270
And the third thing is ego.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:00.710
Ego is who we are,
your own personality.

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.510
All right?

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:06.060
Now, ego as you can
see, is a function--

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:11.220
you know, here we have
three different components

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:13.240
of the nature.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:17.650
And so we have the ego
being the human body itself,

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:21.300
and the human body has
intelligence as a part of it,

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:26.790
which tries to operate, which
tries to make a person move,

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:32.160
make gestures, make speeches,
make movements, eat.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.500
Intellect is
something which helps

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.470
them to organize thoughts.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:41.550
So basically, as you can
see, mind is a part of the--

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.640
between the intelligence
and intellect.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.190
And at those points, mind is a--

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:51.740
and original points, mind
becomes a part of intellect.

00:11:51.740 --> 00:12:01.110
Now this particular ego can
have several attributes.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:03.510
Cosmologically--
cosmologically means

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:08.670
if you transcend this particular
theory to a larger scale,

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:12.480
like, the universe
have a consciousness.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.730
The universe has a nature.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.800
Universe has an intellect.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.540
The universe has
an intelligence.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.170
And the universe has an ego.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.020
If we have an ego which
carries our structure,

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:27.570
the universe structure
has its own ego.

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:33.215
From all that point of view, ego
can have five cosmic elements.

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:37.630
This is, again, old.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:42.100
This is at least 3,000,
4,000-year-old material.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:48.400
But the point is, to create
a model of the universe

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:52.330
into bringing to
the human psyche

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:57.540
and to create a metaphorical
operation in which we

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:00.510
can understand ourselves
by the universe

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:04.440
was this people's
strong contribution.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.120
The five elements
that I note here

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:13.290
are the sky, air,
fire, water, and earth.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:17.430
I do not know whether somebody--
what kind of empirical work

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:22.260
went on to standardize this.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:26.100
Was there any work at
all to say the sky could

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.680
be the first element?

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.460
But as you will see the
material henceforth,

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.920
you will find people
probably did meditate or did

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:38.370
speculate on things and
coming to a conclusion

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:43.670
that if there is a fundamental
element in the universe, that

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:46.160
could be the space.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:47.780
That could be the void.

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:51.720
That could be the creation
of space between objects.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.030
All right?

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:56.320
I think some people who
are familiar with Hinduism

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.680
might also know or might
think that because of that,

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.330
they somehow revered sound.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.880
Sound needs the space to move.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:10.790
So why Hindu people are so
much fascinated with sounds

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:13.940
comes back from these
very, very early thoughts

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:18.380
that the sky, space, becomes
the fundamental element

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:21.850
in the cosmological
universe of the Hindus.

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:28.470
When I say Hindus,
I'm saying the people

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.830
who thought in these
lines and which

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.445
probably continues to be true,
even at the modern times.

00:14:34.445 --> 00:14:35.820
And that's how it
kind of pleases

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:40.560
me to present such material to
and from the cognitive point

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.310
of view.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.360
So sky, air, fire,
water, and earth,

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.920
in this particular order.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:50.220
Sky gives rise to air,
air gives rise to fire,

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:52.270
fire gives way to
water, water gives way

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:56.520
to earth in some kind of
a continuous succession.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:15:02.060
And that is how the
development takes place.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:04.270
Now, one these five elements,
which are orthogonal,

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:07.760
or independent, which are
kind of mutually exclusive,

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.270
they are-- even though one
originates from the other--

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:14.260
once they are in place, they do
not interact with each other.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.430
They are separate.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:22.060
And once they are in place,
they could give rise to,

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:26.620
or to carry the message
of each of these elements,

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:32.740
then human beings or the
so-called beings can create,

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.290
evolutionary way,
create the sense

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:40.610
organs, our sensory perception.

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:43.220
Our sensory perception,
from this point of view,

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:47.510
is designed because of
the cosmic elements,

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:51.850
sensory perceptions being five
and the elements being five.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.600
There's a one-to-one
relationship

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:58.020
between the sensory perception
and the cosmic element.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:10.310
Now the sky space carries sound,
and in order to hear sound,

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:11.125
you have ears.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:18.930
The air carries the
pressure, the molecules,

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:22.070
and in order to get the
feeling of the molecules,

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:24.710
you have the touch
sensation, have the skin.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.150
Similarly, fire
gives you the shape,

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:31.690
the presentation of
material-- the view, so that

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:32.870
gives you the eye.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:38.210
And then the tongue, the
taste, and the nose, the smell.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:42.120
So these five organs
can be created.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.170
Once these five
organs are created,

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:47.270
then these philosophers
will go a little further.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:53.460
And they will say that
human beings are composed

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:58.770
of some more organs,
which are the hands, legs,

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:02.640
the procreation, excretion,
and the speech, the mouth.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.010
And finally, maybe
if you want to have

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:09.030
mind as an exclusive
organ, exclusive element,

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:11.369
you also add mind.

00:17:11.369 --> 00:17:17.470
So this is the Hindu universe,
which even [INAUDIBLE] today,

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:22.599
conceived, developed, probably
somehow empirically debated,

00:17:22.599 --> 00:17:24.760
maybe 3,000, 4,000 years ago.

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:32.870
But when a person is born,
dies, during his life,

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:35.510
somehow people have
this belief that this

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:38.180
is how the body is
composed of, and this

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:42.000
is how the body will deal with.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.840
The principal part of it, I
must say, in this whole thing,

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:50.520
that all these
so-called developments,

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:54.150
they took place from
the right-hand element,

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.860
which is the nature.

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:58.920
The consciousness
did not interact

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.540
with all the development.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.790
The consciousness is an entity.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:04.710
Nature is an entity.

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:08.160
And this nature, through
its own processes,

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:13.080
develops the various elements
and then organs and eventually

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:17.455
beings, and beings become
human beings, and so on.

00:18:17.455 --> 00:18:17.955
okay.

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:26.000
If that's so, then what happens?

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:30.400
At this time, they
will think about that

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:35.370
suppose that consciousness
is endowed in all beings,

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:39.030
and they are the guiding
factors in all beings,

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:43.620
so naturally, there is a element
of consciousness in all beings.

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:49.200
This particular thought,
which eventually we

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:52.380
have called soul or something,
which Aristotle accepts--

00:18:52.380 --> 00:19:03.030
and I think generally we have
become addicted to a system

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:06.120
that, yes, we have a soul.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.270
And soul is the one
which God [INAUDIBLE]..

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:14.170
The soul is the one which
understands, suffers.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:19.390
Soul is the one which probably
eventually takes our life

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:20.970
wherever it needs to go.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:24.630
Some kind of religious
thoughts have

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:27.120
been associated with the soul.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:31.770
Originally, however, these
people did not think that way.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:37.900
They thought the soul would be
an element of consciousness.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:42.190
And because consciousness
does not transform--

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:46.600
oh, by the way, when I say
consciousness and nature,

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.730
and from the point of
view of the time scales

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:50.860
I was talking about, all right?

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:55.660
So nature, because it evolves,
it has a shorter time scale,

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:58.060
because these
things evolve, form.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:19:59.290
They might change.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:03.930
But consciousness has a
much, much larger time

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:07.640
scale, most likely
doesn't change at all,

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:09.380
from the original theory.

00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:14.240
Now coming back here now,
so the soul would be, then,

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:16.520
an element of consciousness.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:18.590
And because the
original consciousness

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:23.300
has a very long time scale, the
individual soul's consciousness

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.410
will also have a
strong time scale.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:32.170
What follows because
of that, from the point

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:33.530
of view of the body--

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:38.530
when the body decays, body dies,
this time scale of the soul

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:41.020
is longer than the body.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:44.290
So it might look as though
the soul is immortal.

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:47.740
It might look as though
the soul doesn't die,

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:51.170
and soul remains
in the universe.

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:53.120
Once created,
doesn't go anywhere.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:56.430
It stays in the universe.

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:59.300
What does it do?

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:04.600
It becomes what they
call a passive witness.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:06.720
Why becomes passive?

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:14.940
It's a passive witness, passive
witness because it doesn't act.

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.320
I must tell you also
one more thing here.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:19.940
During this particular
discussion about the Hindu

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:24.100
cosmology, or the time of
these philosophical discourses

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:28.820
on this, the question of
time strongly came in.

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.860
And people thought
the definition of time

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:35.640
would be something
that differentiates.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:36.870
The object is there.

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.360
The object has moved.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:39.910
The position has changed.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:40.470
See?

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:43.170
There's a different
realization has come in.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:45.840
And that will kind of
make you feel that as

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:48.900
though some time has elapsed.

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:55.420
So from that point of
view, because the soul

00:21:55.420 --> 00:22:02.450
has a long time scale,
so it should not react.

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:04.670
Even though my hand
moves, my mouth

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:06.620
speaks, even though
I have personally

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.520
moved, my soul is
not moving with me,

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:15.120
because it operates on
a longer time scale.

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:15.620
All right?

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:20.210
So it basically-- because
of that, it will stay inert.

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:27.130
So once we define this, once we
make this particular framework,

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:31.900
then we come to the experiments
that people have done lately.

00:22:31.900 --> 00:22:36.520
And I want to project them
in view of Shankara's work.

00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:43.730
Those experiments have shown,
I think, the following.

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:52.930
These are accepted by
the Indian philosophers.

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:55.330
And I think lately the
different experiments

00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:57.580
in Europe and this
country have come

00:22:57.580 --> 00:22:59.920
to such kind of conclusion.

00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:03.910
That is, we do operate
on different brain waves.

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:08.290
We do operate on different
kinds of systematic cognition

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:13.420
on our brain function, depending
upon how we exercise our brain,

00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:16.810
depending upon how intensely
the brain is working,

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:18.880
how relaxed the brain is.

00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:20.890
The concept that
these people have

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:24.280
from the point of view
of their own thinking

00:23:24.280 --> 00:23:26.620
that the consciousness--

00:23:26.620 --> 00:23:30.200
which I said soul,
which I said is

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:33.470
a part of universal
consciousness--

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:40.690
may exist in four
quantum states.

00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:46.660
One state is as we are, waking,
which is very strongly-- if you

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:50.380
take the brain images, you
will find that the brain

00:23:50.380 --> 00:23:52.730
is functioning pretty fast.

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:59.800
Brain is functioning, what,
about 20 cycles of second.

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:03.230
It's kind of very
strongly operating,

00:24:03.230 --> 00:24:05.630
because different kinds
of sensory perceptions

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:08.540
are coming to the brain,
different kinds of ideas coming

00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:10.760
to the brain, and you
are dealing with all

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:13.480
the different functionalities.

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:17.830
Then you come to the
dream, which kind

00:24:17.830 --> 00:24:22.900
of semi-awake, but not really
fully cognizant of everything

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:23.980
that's going on.

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:27.160
You are slept, but
not fully slept.

00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:31.660
In that situation, the brain
has slowed down considerably.

00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.990
It probably has gone down to
about eight cycles a second.

00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:38.770
And also, people know that as
you close your eyes and so on,

00:24:38.770 --> 00:24:43.240
you can possibly see these
different images, visions,

00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:46.300
and so on, which is a part
of the whole cyclic process

00:24:46.300 --> 00:24:50.200
the brain goes through when the
brain is somewhat slowed down,

00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:55.210
not as compared to the
completely awake state.

00:24:55.210 --> 00:24:56.980
Then there are two
other steps, which

00:24:56.980 --> 00:25:01.330
are the sleeping
state, which is kind

00:25:01.330 --> 00:25:12.500
of the original thought of the
soul that the person is living.

00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:16.040
And however, simply
the body is sleeping.

00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:20.285
That means that the
person's life is not really

00:25:20.285 --> 00:25:21.620
fully gone away.

00:25:21.620 --> 00:25:24.080
Person's senses are
not fully gone away.

00:25:24.080 --> 00:25:26.750
And the soul is only active.

00:25:26.750 --> 00:25:28.930
So in that state, people say--

00:25:28.930 --> 00:25:31.920
like we have the delta
wave, which is the one cycle

00:25:31.920 --> 00:25:34.480
a second and so on,
which is operating

00:25:34.480 --> 00:25:39.690
on your brain functioning.

00:25:39.690 --> 00:25:41.790
However, the fourth
state, which I

00:25:41.790 --> 00:25:45.420
call the awakened state,
for which these people talk

00:25:45.420 --> 00:25:48.600
about very strongly,
and I can't really

00:25:48.600 --> 00:25:53.400
give a good example of what an
awakened state might look like,

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:55.830
except I will kind of
comment the following.

00:25:55.830 --> 00:26:00.720
I will say that when you
are strongly focused, when

00:26:00.720 --> 00:26:05.630
attention is
concentrated, when you

00:26:05.630 --> 00:26:12.210
are dealing with a particular
process with utmost sincerity,

00:26:12.210 --> 00:26:17.040
where as though your
whole senses are focused

00:26:17.040 --> 00:26:23.450
on that particular object, it
is either to rescue a person,

00:26:23.450 --> 00:26:31.970
saving your own child, helping
your friend in strong distress,

00:26:31.970 --> 00:26:37.700
or being very lonely yourself
on any particular problem,

00:26:37.700 --> 00:26:41.930
where you are
deeply to yourself--

00:26:41.930 --> 00:26:46.190
so I think such kind of states,
which can happen momentarily

00:26:46.190 --> 00:26:51.680
to us, where we don't really get
cognizance of all of our senses

00:26:51.680 --> 00:26:54.410
at all, because
they're so focused--

00:26:54.410 --> 00:26:56.390
or even for students
and so on when you're

00:26:56.390 --> 00:26:58.220
doing your homework
for tomorrow, when

00:26:58.220 --> 00:27:00.320
the exam is there and so
on, and you don't really

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:02.680
care what's going on around--

00:27:02.680 --> 00:27:06.620
so that could be a state
where you are fully, fully,

00:27:06.620 --> 00:27:10.635
fully, fully conscious
of only yourself.

00:27:15.830 --> 00:27:21.380
And not receiving this
sensory input from anywhere.

00:27:21.380 --> 00:27:24.700
What happens in such situation--
it could be, I think,

00:27:24.700 --> 00:27:27.690
no experiments have been done--

00:27:27.690 --> 00:27:32.040
would be that probably, you
don't have a wave at all.

00:27:32.040 --> 00:27:34.230
You will simply
have a DC current.

00:27:34.230 --> 00:27:39.780
You will simply have a situation
where you will have a full--

00:27:39.780 --> 00:27:41.790
the brain is functioning,
but brain not

00:27:41.790 --> 00:27:44.070
functioning in an
undulating manner,

00:27:44.070 --> 00:27:48.940
but brain is functioning
as though it is steady,

00:27:48.940 --> 00:27:54.280
as though it is operating
with full attention.

00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:59.830
Now, such particular thought,
such particular state, Shankara

00:27:59.830 --> 00:28:02.200
will deal very strongly with.

00:28:02.200 --> 00:28:04.780
Let me now come to Shankara.

00:28:04.780 --> 00:28:11.350
Oh, before I come, I want
to put two more words here,

00:28:11.350 --> 00:28:17.050
that in this theory
that we have,

00:28:17.050 --> 00:28:21.040
because this consciousness
can be all around us,

00:28:21.040 --> 00:28:25.100
consciousness can take two
different manifestations,

00:28:25.100 --> 00:28:27.510
or what are called
manifest consciousness,

00:28:27.510 --> 00:28:29.410
unmanifest consciousness.

00:28:29.410 --> 00:28:30.600
And then people have--

00:28:30.600 --> 00:28:32.960
Hindus have called them gods.

00:28:32.960 --> 00:28:34.660
Hindus have called them--

00:28:34.660 --> 00:28:37.180
you know, like when
somebody has endowed

00:28:37.180 --> 00:28:41.440
with strong consciousness,
where he's cognizing everything

00:28:41.440 --> 00:28:45.640
easily, quickly, strongly,
has strong values

00:28:45.640 --> 00:28:49.480
and so on, they have been
associated with godly nature

00:28:49.480 --> 00:28:51.130
in this particular philosophy.

00:28:51.130 --> 00:28:55.360
But in general, also, the
confines consciousness

00:28:55.360 --> 00:29:00.370
may be all around us, but
doesn't manifest itself

00:29:00.370 --> 00:29:01.487
as a physical object.

00:29:01.487 --> 00:29:03.070
You see, and you
must understand this,

00:29:03.070 --> 00:29:06.310
even though that
consciousness do manifest

00:29:06.310 --> 00:29:09.280
as a physical object, it
is not associated itself

00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:12.050
with some nature.

00:29:12.050 --> 00:29:15.230
And so consciousness
may not manifest at all,

00:29:15.230 --> 00:29:19.310
but may be present
all around us.

00:29:19.310 --> 00:29:21.470
And that, we can call God.

00:29:21.470 --> 00:29:24.590
Or we can call God
something where

00:29:24.590 --> 00:29:28.190
an embodiment of
consciousness did take place

00:29:28.190 --> 00:29:32.710
and which kind of went through
the normal, natural cycle

00:29:32.710 --> 00:29:36.000
controlled by the nature.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:42.110
So this brings us to our
philosopher friend, Shankara.

00:29:42.110 --> 00:29:46.016
Shankara-- who is Shankara?

00:29:46.016 --> 00:29:51.500
He lived around 800
AD, a prolific writer.

00:29:51.500 --> 00:29:54.650
And what we know so far--

00:29:54.650 --> 00:29:56.570
that he's a strong debater.

00:29:56.570 --> 00:29:59.780
Debater because when you
make some thoughts which

00:29:59.780 --> 00:30:03.740
may be somewhat different than
what the establishment thinks

00:30:03.740 --> 00:30:05.450
at a particular
time, some people

00:30:05.450 --> 00:30:07.100
might try to argue with you.

00:30:07.100 --> 00:30:08.900
So he was probably--

00:30:08.900 --> 00:30:12.320
spent most of his time
in debating his views

00:30:12.320 --> 00:30:13.970
with the other people.

00:30:13.970 --> 00:30:17.750
Most people at that point
were Buddhists, Buddhists

00:30:17.750 --> 00:30:20.480
who would not really--

00:30:20.480 --> 00:30:23.354
who'll think-- I'll say
what the difference is.

00:30:23.354 --> 00:30:24.770
But basically the
difference would

00:30:24.770 --> 00:30:28.100
be that whether
our consciousness,

00:30:28.100 --> 00:30:30.530
our understanding, our
cognition, our intellect,

00:30:30.530 --> 00:30:33.440
is controlled by
us, or our intellect

00:30:33.440 --> 00:30:39.690
is controlled by or helped by,
assisted by, a consciousness

00:30:39.690 --> 00:30:42.680
which is larger than us.

00:30:42.680 --> 00:30:44.520
That's the principal difference.

00:30:44.520 --> 00:30:47.230
And as you'll see,
Shankara will argue now

00:30:47.230 --> 00:30:49.760
that that particular--

00:30:49.760 --> 00:30:55.400
the intellect operates, but
intellect is endowed always

00:30:55.400 --> 00:30:58.760
with this blessing of
large consciousness

00:30:58.760 --> 00:31:03.040
from which it draws
its resources.

00:31:03.040 --> 00:31:04.620
How does it do it?

00:31:04.620 --> 00:31:06.960
He defines three terms.

00:31:06.960 --> 00:31:10.320
He defines something
called a knower, something

00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:13.850
called knowledge,
something called known.

00:31:13.850 --> 00:31:21.240
So knower is the actor, the
one which does, one which sees,

00:31:21.240 --> 00:31:27.780
one which hears, one which
remembers, one which decides.

00:31:27.780 --> 00:31:29.950
So that's the knower.

00:31:29.950 --> 00:31:32.520
So in all cognition
process, Shankara

00:31:32.520 --> 00:31:37.570
will say that something, a
quantity, called knower exists.

00:31:37.570 --> 00:31:41.400
So the question is, can
we find what the knower is

00:31:41.400 --> 00:31:45.370
in our body-mind-nature system?

00:31:45.370 --> 00:31:48.300
Knowledge is easy.

00:31:48.300 --> 00:31:50.900
We know that whenever
we try to know

00:31:50.900 --> 00:31:57.100
things or search for things,
or we can search always

00:31:57.100 --> 00:31:58.900
for knowledge.

00:31:58.900 --> 00:32:01.000
And knowledge we acquire.

00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:03.030
But I'll come in a
second where Shankara

00:32:03.030 --> 00:32:04.810
will think about knowledge.

00:32:04.810 --> 00:32:07.054
And then finally, known.

00:32:07.054 --> 00:32:10.400
Known is your
accumulated knowledge.

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:13.330
Known is your decision process.

00:32:13.330 --> 00:32:17.560
Known is how much you
can really reach out

00:32:17.560 --> 00:32:20.830
to your own consciousness
and knowledge

00:32:20.830 --> 00:32:25.600
to associate new objects
into that knowledge.

00:32:25.600 --> 00:32:28.960
And this come the
catch, Shankara's catch.

00:32:28.960 --> 00:32:31.360
What is Shankara's catch?

00:32:31.360 --> 00:32:41.470
It is-- oh, before I do,
that three definitions.

00:32:41.470 --> 00:32:43.960
What's the knower?

00:32:43.960 --> 00:32:46.190
Knower uses the intellect.

00:32:46.190 --> 00:32:49.780
Mind you, again, we have
defined intellect, intelligence,

00:32:49.780 --> 00:32:50.830
and ego.

00:32:50.830 --> 00:32:54.860
So knower uses intellect.

00:32:54.860 --> 00:32:57.440
That we can know.

00:32:57.440 --> 00:33:02.620
In order to know anything,
we have to discriminate.

00:33:02.620 --> 00:33:08.320
We have to use our collected
knowledge to disseminate,

00:33:08.320 --> 00:33:13.720
to decipher what's up there.

00:33:13.720 --> 00:33:17.420
What Shankara will
say different, though,

00:33:17.420 --> 00:33:22.020
that this particular
cognition is

00:33:22.020 --> 00:33:28.570
a superposition of the
consciousness on the intellect.

00:33:28.570 --> 00:33:32.470
That is, the intellect is
looking for a solution.

00:33:32.470 --> 00:33:35.290
Intellect is looking
for assimilation.

00:33:35.290 --> 00:33:39.640
Intellect is looking for adding
the stuff to the accumulated

00:33:39.640 --> 00:33:41.330
knowledge.

00:33:41.330 --> 00:33:43.700
But intellect is
not sufficiently

00:33:43.700 --> 00:33:47.940
aware to find out everything
about the new object.

00:33:47.940 --> 00:33:52.700
So unless intellect
is conscious,

00:33:52.700 --> 00:33:55.870
intellect will fail to operate.

00:33:55.870 --> 00:33:57.580
Intellect is biological.

00:33:57.580 --> 00:33:59.280
Intellect's part of nature.

00:33:59.280 --> 00:34:01.240
Intellect is part of the body.

00:34:01.240 --> 00:34:06.550
And that has to associate itself
with the consciousness in order

00:34:06.550 --> 00:34:14.560
to make itself cognize the
object that it receives.

00:34:14.560 --> 00:34:20.100
So this is Shankara's
first hypothesis on knower.

00:34:20.100 --> 00:34:26.840
Then, knowledge is a
perception of the intellect.

00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:28.560
We all perceive.

00:34:28.560 --> 00:34:31.219
We all have our own
ideas about things.

00:34:31.219 --> 00:34:34.310
So he agrees with that, that
you can have your own theories.

00:34:34.310 --> 00:34:37.340
You can have your own feelings
about various objects,

00:34:37.340 --> 00:34:40.130
various motions,
various functions.

00:34:40.130 --> 00:34:43.730
But he says you have
to then go beyond that

00:34:43.730 --> 00:34:50.290
and to see how much of that
knowledge is universal.

00:34:50.290 --> 00:34:53.420
Is that knowledge strictly
to yourself, or anybody

00:34:53.420 --> 00:34:56.500
else agrees with you?

00:34:56.500 --> 00:34:58.990
In order to make that
particular transition,

00:34:58.990 --> 00:35:02.110
Shankara will go a very,
very long step forward,

00:35:02.110 --> 00:35:04.480
will say that all
knowledge, if they

00:35:04.480 --> 00:35:09.010
be classified of knowledge,
they have to be true.

00:35:09.010 --> 00:35:11.440
They have to be true.

00:35:11.440 --> 00:35:13.520
They must have a value.

00:35:13.520 --> 00:35:16.810
They must have a value
which is not transient.

00:35:16.810 --> 00:35:19.640
Remember, I said the time scale.

00:35:19.640 --> 00:35:23.840
So it would not be a small
time scale operation,

00:35:23.840 --> 00:35:27.230
but end knowledge,
if you know it,

00:35:27.230 --> 00:35:31.720
has a time scale much larger
than your perception time

00:35:31.720 --> 00:35:34.470
scale.

00:35:34.470 --> 00:35:37.630
He will say, look, every
time the sensory organs

00:35:37.630 --> 00:35:41.980
operating and you are receiving
information, creating images,

00:35:41.980 --> 00:35:44.620
you are trying to think
the images are stable

00:35:44.620 --> 00:35:49.480
because of persistence, because
of the new image has something

00:35:49.480 --> 00:35:50.980
with the old image,
and you did not

00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:54.920
distinguish the new
image and the old image.

00:35:54.920 --> 00:35:58.490
However, whether
there is truth in it

00:35:58.490 --> 00:36:02.206
is a function of if the
image lasts for pretty,

00:36:02.206 --> 00:36:04.590
pretty, pretty long time.

00:36:04.590 --> 00:36:08.720
And that you can only do
because your intellect is only

00:36:08.720 --> 00:36:10.790
operating a short time scale.

00:36:10.790 --> 00:36:15.170
You associate that with the
long time scale consciousness

00:36:15.170 --> 00:36:17.720
such that you can
see, yes, there

00:36:17.720 --> 00:36:19.790
is truth in this particular
feeling, the truth

00:36:19.790 --> 00:36:21.350
in this particular
message, the truth

00:36:21.350 --> 00:36:22.880
in this particular thought.

00:36:26.640 --> 00:36:33.220
Because of this, he will make
this second assertion, that is,

00:36:33.220 --> 00:36:37.810
our intellect is not capable
of finding the truth.

00:36:37.810 --> 00:36:41.740
Our body intellect is not
capable of finding the truth,

00:36:41.740 --> 00:36:45.640
because body intellect is
conditioned by the body

00:36:45.640 --> 00:36:49.210
experiences, is conditioned
by the knowledge

00:36:49.210 --> 00:36:51.760
that we see before,
is conditioned

00:36:51.760 --> 00:36:56.470
by the accumulation of
material that it has received.

00:36:56.470 --> 00:37:00.510
Hence, it is not
capable of deciphering

00:37:00.510 --> 00:37:03.150
information which
is new to it, which

00:37:03.150 --> 00:37:07.470
means when the child starts up,
whether he will start smiling

00:37:07.470 --> 00:37:12.420
or crying is a function of
the child's intellect, is

00:37:12.420 --> 00:37:15.810
a function of consciousness
which the child's

00:37:15.810 --> 00:37:18.070
intellect interacts with.

00:37:18.070 --> 00:37:21.990
And then the intellect receives
the message that, look,

00:37:21.990 --> 00:37:23.220
smiling is good for you.

00:37:26.960 --> 00:37:29.570
Similar hypothesis,
similar hypothesis

00:37:29.570 --> 00:37:34.130
that when we have
a decision to make,

00:37:34.130 --> 00:37:36.860
our intellect is
incapable of getting

00:37:36.860 --> 00:37:39.910
into the depth of the
problem and making us

00:37:39.910 --> 00:37:44.190
feel assisted on the problem.

00:37:44.190 --> 00:37:47.830
And then the intellect
searches for--

00:37:47.830 --> 00:37:49.800
and when the intellect
searches for, it's

00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:52.260
the consciousness
which kind of then

00:37:52.260 --> 00:37:57.654
helps the intellect, okay, hey,
look, there's the solution.

00:37:57.654 --> 00:37:59.570
Now, this consciousness,
whether the intellect

00:37:59.570 --> 00:38:02.730
can reach it or not,
that's up to the intellect.

00:38:02.730 --> 00:38:06.720
But the theory is that
that consciousness exists,

00:38:06.720 --> 00:38:09.585
and intellect can
reach out, all right?

00:38:09.585 --> 00:38:14.190
And I'll come in a minute,
how do you reach out?

00:38:14.190 --> 00:38:17.130
And then known, so
he will say what's

00:38:17.130 --> 00:38:21.324
known is a function of evidence,
is a function of inference,

00:38:21.324 --> 00:38:23.490
and function of articulation,
whether you can really

00:38:23.490 --> 00:38:25.100
speak it, right?

00:38:25.100 --> 00:38:27.240
So known is--
that's kind of easy.

00:38:27.240 --> 00:38:31.130
That's easy, because you
know you can always state it.

00:38:31.130 --> 00:38:37.600
But then when you say words,
all right, by showing images,

00:38:37.600 --> 00:38:40.240
by comparing-- this man is a
man because the man has two legs

00:38:40.240 --> 00:38:43.220
and so on, two hand and
stands erect and so on--

00:38:43.220 --> 00:38:45.080
so that's like evidence.

00:38:45.080 --> 00:38:47.910
But when you say, the man--

00:38:47.910 --> 00:38:51.580
I describe this person by
having seen this person,

00:38:51.580 --> 00:38:55.930
using words, that gives me a
different kind of cognition,

00:38:55.930 --> 00:39:00.230
because I don't know so
much about the person.

00:39:00.230 --> 00:39:02.900
I will describe the
person as I see it,

00:39:02.900 --> 00:39:05.000
which is not the full story.

00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:08.720
And hence, I must be
consciously intellectually

00:39:08.720 --> 00:39:13.240
active, blessed with this
overall consciousness

00:39:13.240 --> 00:39:18.720
to help me, to stabilize
what I know about the things

00:39:18.720 --> 00:39:21.840
so that I can articulate.

00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:28.680
So this is the story about the
knower, knowledge, and known.

00:39:28.680 --> 00:39:36.960
Then he will say that
because of this dilemma,

00:39:36.960 --> 00:39:47.660
that intellect is only limited
by the human experience,

00:39:47.660 --> 00:39:51.570
by the human thoughts
or by the human memory.

00:39:51.570 --> 00:40:01.810
So the first paradox would be,
we will never know the knower.

00:40:05.840 --> 00:40:09.770
In other words, you know that
your intellect functions.

00:40:09.770 --> 00:40:13.040
You know that your intellect
helps you understand.

00:40:13.040 --> 00:40:18.370
But you do not know how
that intellect functions.

00:40:18.370 --> 00:40:21.460
The intellect has
function by virtue

00:40:21.460 --> 00:40:26.050
of consciousness, which
has assisted in gaining

00:40:26.050 --> 00:40:28.090
the particular cognition.

00:40:28.090 --> 00:40:32.590
And because you have no
access to the consciousness,

00:40:32.590 --> 00:40:35.350
hence you--

00:40:35.350 --> 00:40:39.300
it is beyond the intellect.

00:40:39.300 --> 00:40:40.900
And because it's
beyond intellect,

00:40:40.900 --> 00:40:43.330
intellect doesn't perceive it.

00:40:43.330 --> 00:40:46.055
intellect only feels it.

00:40:46.055 --> 00:40:50.860
Shankara's metaphor
is it's like light.

00:40:50.860 --> 00:40:52.940
The consciousness is like light.

00:40:52.940 --> 00:40:55.490
So light's something
that you don't see,

00:40:55.490 --> 00:40:59.140
but you only feel it
when light falls on you.

00:40:59.140 --> 00:41:02.510
So it's some kind of
metaphor, similar metaphor,

00:41:02.510 --> 00:41:06.350
where he would say that knower
is outside the intellect.

00:41:06.350 --> 00:41:08.660
And hence, you are, with
your intellectual energy,

00:41:08.660 --> 00:41:10.880
you are not able to.

00:41:10.880 --> 00:41:14.960
And because you can't
see it, all cognition

00:41:14.960 --> 00:41:17.720
is always incomplete.

00:41:17.720 --> 00:41:19.770
All right?

00:41:19.770 --> 00:41:22.640
Why is incomplete?

00:41:22.640 --> 00:41:26.282
It's incomplete because you
don't know who lets you know.

00:41:29.114 --> 00:41:31.510
You have some knowledge.

00:41:31.510 --> 00:41:33.260
You did find a solution.

00:41:33.260 --> 00:41:37.190
You did complete your
local cognition cycle.

00:41:37.190 --> 00:41:39.970
But you did not know how
that consciousness, how

00:41:39.970 --> 00:41:42.820
that local cycle
did get complete.

00:41:42.820 --> 00:41:46.750
And because of that,
cognition remains.

00:41:46.750 --> 00:41:50.980
So then he will hypothesize two
very fundamental hypotheses,

00:41:50.980 --> 00:41:54.430
which comes
Shankara's philosophy.

00:41:54.430 --> 00:42:02.390
The first one is that
any knowledge that you

00:42:02.390 --> 00:42:07.850
ought to know, you
must know the knower.

00:42:07.850 --> 00:42:10.960
It is the knower
which helped you

00:42:10.960 --> 00:42:20.220
cognize through your
intellect, assisted you.

00:42:20.220 --> 00:42:24.650
So if you have any
search for knowledge,

00:42:24.650 --> 00:42:30.860
then you search for the knower.

00:42:30.860 --> 00:42:36.960
And knowledge is consciousness.

00:42:36.960 --> 00:42:39.140
Knower is knowledge,
and knowledge

00:42:39.140 --> 00:42:42.540
itself is consciousness.

00:42:42.540 --> 00:42:47.280
What it means now-- which means
that every thought, every idea,

00:42:47.280 --> 00:42:55.200
every cognition, is endowed
with an intellectual curiosity.

00:42:55.200 --> 00:43:03.080
But that curiosity is not
complete till a consciousness--

00:43:03.080 --> 00:43:07.340
a conscious effort has
been made to cognize.

00:43:07.340 --> 00:43:11.480
And that conscious effort is
not within your discretion,

00:43:11.480 --> 00:43:14.090
but it is a pure connection.

00:43:14.090 --> 00:43:15.690
It's a pure grace.

00:43:15.690 --> 00:43:20.720
It is a pure assistance by
the universal consciousness

00:43:20.720 --> 00:43:24.410
onto intellect.

00:43:24.410 --> 00:43:25.010
So you know.

00:43:28.080 --> 00:43:30.070
So these are the two hypotheses.

00:43:30.070 --> 00:43:32.070
Once he has the
hypothesis, I will kind of

00:43:32.070 --> 00:43:37.690
say that he'll go
a step further.

00:43:37.690 --> 00:43:39.480
And he will say that, look--

00:43:46.840 --> 00:43:58.240
he will conclude-- that,
look, you have intelligence.

00:43:58.240 --> 00:44:01.370
You know, I titled my talk
"Intelligence and God."

00:44:01.370 --> 00:44:09.600
So he will say that, look,
your intelligence guides you

00:44:09.600 --> 00:44:14.160
in search of knowledge,
search of knowing things.

00:44:14.160 --> 00:44:18.350
But your-- the way you should
guide your intelligence is to--

00:44:25.190 --> 00:44:27.130
your intelligence is
in search of knowledge,

00:44:27.130 --> 00:44:31.060
but intelligence limited by
your perception and delusion.

00:44:31.060 --> 00:44:33.730
Delusion is a word which
we'll use very strongly.

00:44:33.730 --> 00:44:36.070
That is, you think you know.

00:44:36.070 --> 00:44:37.690
You think you are.

00:44:37.690 --> 00:44:40.250
You have cognized the
object completely.

00:44:40.250 --> 00:44:42.310
But that's an illusion.

00:44:42.310 --> 00:44:42.880
That's it.

00:44:42.880 --> 00:44:43.900
You are deluded.

00:44:43.900 --> 00:44:46.870
You're deluded because
your body, your senses,

00:44:46.870 --> 00:44:48.040
have failed you.

00:44:48.040 --> 00:44:49.810
They have kind of
given you an impression

00:44:49.810 --> 00:44:53.440
which is a local, transient,
momentary, very short time

00:44:53.440 --> 00:44:54.180
scale.

00:44:54.180 --> 00:44:57.730
So in order to make a larger
time scale, more permanent,

00:44:57.730 --> 00:45:01.540
have stronger, stable
knowledge, you must search more.

00:45:01.540 --> 00:45:04.930
And if you search more, then
you try to get the knowledge.

00:45:04.930 --> 00:45:08.620
If you get the
knowledge, however, you

00:45:08.620 --> 00:45:12.820
can't get the full knowledge
unless you know the knower.

00:45:12.820 --> 00:45:15.466
Who is the knower?

00:45:15.466 --> 00:45:18.890
He is knowledge.

00:45:18.890 --> 00:45:22.430
So the ultimate
knowledge is the knower.

00:45:22.430 --> 00:45:24.860
And that-- I did
not use the word--

00:45:24.860 --> 00:45:27.470
he will use a word
called Brahman.

00:45:27.470 --> 00:45:29.240
So he will say
that, look, there's

00:45:29.240 --> 00:45:32.540
only one truth in the universe.

00:45:32.540 --> 00:45:37.130
That is this cosmic,
ultimate consciousness

00:45:37.130 --> 00:45:42.050
that you call Brahman, which
is pervading every object

00:45:42.050 --> 00:45:44.720
everywhere, all over the place.

00:45:44.720 --> 00:45:49.160
And then that helps
you intellectually

00:45:49.160 --> 00:45:54.260
to gain understanding
of various objects.

00:45:54.260 --> 00:46:01.010
What it has to do with
machine intelligence

00:46:01.010 --> 00:46:06.730
is the machines will know.

00:46:06.730 --> 00:46:08.750
Machines know them objectively.

00:46:08.750 --> 00:46:11.290
Machines don't perceive.

00:46:11.290 --> 00:46:13.900
Machines tell you
what the facts are.

00:46:13.900 --> 00:46:17.630
So we can train the
machines to really go

00:46:17.630 --> 00:46:23.690
become smarter and
smarter and then

00:46:23.690 --> 00:46:28.030
be consciously
objective, knowledge

00:46:28.030 --> 00:46:31.550
being all parts
of consciousness.

00:46:31.550 --> 00:46:35.110
So all the knowledge
that we know consciously,

00:46:35.110 --> 00:46:38.440
which had been endowed
through consciousness to us,

00:46:38.440 --> 00:46:41.050
if we accumulate
together, maybe we

00:46:41.050 --> 00:46:46.900
can asymptotically reach
this large consciousness.

00:46:46.900 --> 00:46:48.804
Thank you.

00:46:48.804 --> 00:46:51.792
[APPLAUSE]

00:46:56.274 --> 00:46:58.979
She said I must stop at 5:20
so that I can take questions,

00:46:58.979 --> 00:46:59.520
so I stopped.

00:46:59.520 --> 00:46:59.790
5:20.

00:46:59.790 --> 00:47:00.694
I take questions.

00:47:00.694 --> 00:47:02.610
FOERST: Yeah, we have
some time for questions.

00:47:02.610 --> 00:47:03.630
Thank you very much.

00:47:03.630 --> 00:47:05.400
For me, actually,
that was very new.

00:47:05.400 --> 00:47:09.420
I've never did anything with
Hinduism, so I'm fascinated.

00:47:09.420 --> 00:47:11.040
And I'm actually
especially fascinated

00:47:11.040 --> 00:47:13.417
when I have the right to kind
of ask the first question

00:47:13.417 --> 00:47:14.500
or give the first comment.

00:47:14.500 --> 00:47:14.860
MISRA: Please do.

00:47:14.860 --> 00:47:15.510
Please do.

00:47:15.510 --> 00:47:18.420
FOERST: How close that is
to this whole Western idea

00:47:18.420 --> 00:47:19.710
of this whole--

00:47:19.710 --> 00:47:21.930
first of all, the
whole body-mind split

00:47:21.930 --> 00:47:24.180
and the whole
subjectivity-objectivity

00:47:24.180 --> 00:47:25.450
dilemma.

00:47:25.450 --> 00:47:25.950
MISRA: Yes.

00:47:25.950 --> 00:47:27.600
FOERST: And I would like to--

00:47:27.600 --> 00:47:28.770
if that's--

00:47:28.770 --> 00:47:30.990
MISRA: The point is
it doesn't contradict

00:47:30.990 --> 00:47:35.150
what happens the following, like
the modern psychological theory

00:47:35.150 --> 00:47:38.460
that, how does our
intelligence operate?

00:47:38.460 --> 00:47:40.290
I think I used
those words before.

00:47:40.290 --> 00:47:42.360
But it operates in three modes--

00:47:42.360 --> 00:47:46.410
assimilation,
accommodation, organization.

00:47:46.410 --> 00:47:51.930
Assimilation is a function
of the brain, intellect.

00:47:51.930 --> 00:47:54.900
The accommodation is a
function of the mind.

00:47:54.900 --> 00:47:57.790
And organization,
function of the memory.

00:47:57.790 --> 00:48:02.400
What he's saying, that
these whole three processes,

00:48:02.400 --> 00:48:06.050
even though they
look biological,

00:48:06.050 --> 00:48:07.460
they are not biological.

00:48:07.460 --> 00:48:09.500
They are conscious.

00:48:09.500 --> 00:48:12.980
That you are only
limited by your biology,

00:48:12.980 --> 00:48:16.310
by your body structure, by
your memory, by your brain,

00:48:16.310 --> 00:48:19.940
to receive the knowledge
as much as you can gain,

00:48:19.940 --> 00:48:23.120
as much as you
can really obtain.

00:48:23.120 --> 00:48:29.750
So what you do is, if you stay
in a so-called awakened state,

00:48:29.750 --> 00:48:33.040
where your mind
is fully focused,

00:48:33.040 --> 00:48:36.900
where your cognition is
total, at that point,

00:48:36.900 --> 00:48:40.970
you will see that the
knowledge that comes to you

00:48:40.970 --> 00:48:43.100
is only the pure knowledge.

00:48:43.100 --> 00:48:47.360
But what happens, though,
people who have written about it

00:48:47.360 --> 00:48:49.820
and people who have probably
reached such a state,

00:48:49.820 --> 00:48:52.730
they will say at
that point, you don't

00:48:52.730 --> 00:48:56.190
distinguish between objects.

00:48:56.190 --> 00:48:57.560
So that's the catch there.

00:48:57.560 --> 00:48:59.840
The catch is that
once you have--

00:48:59.840 --> 00:49:01.880
you don't have undulations.

00:49:01.880 --> 00:49:05.090
When the times become still--

00:49:05.090 --> 00:49:09.520
you understand?-- when the
differentiation doesn't exist,

00:49:09.520 --> 00:49:15.530
then things become
cognitively indifferent.

00:49:15.530 --> 00:49:19.749
And hence you don't have
any physical perception,

00:49:19.749 --> 00:49:21.290
because you have
suspend your senses.

00:49:24.400 --> 00:49:26.100
So that's the dilemma there.

00:49:26.100 --> 00:49:28.420
That is, one can probably
reach such a state,

00:49:28.420 --> 00:49:33.460
but you must have some kind of
your natural perception still

00:49:33.460 --> 00:49:37.860
continuing so that
you can receive

00:49:37.860 --> 00:49:41.360
this so-called understanding
that you are trying to receive.

00:49:41.360 --> 00:49:43.350
Otherwise, you are
towards the god,

00:49:43.350 --> 00:49:47.450
or you have reached a point
where your senses are not

00:49:47.450 --> 00:49:49.157
really important anymore.

00:49:49.157 --> 00:49:50.740
The only thing that's
important to you

00:49:50.740 --> 00:49:54.530
or has been important to
you only is this flat field

00:49:54.530 --> 00:49:56.766
consciousness.

00:49:56.766 --> 00:49:57.266
Yes?

00:50:02.600 --> 00:50:05.000
AUDIENCE: Without
nature, consciousness

00:50:05.000 --> 00:50:06.310
is still in existence.

00:50:06.310 --> 00:50:07.300
MISRA: Yes.

00:50:07.300 --> 00:50:09.690
FOERST: Would you mind repeating
the questions for the--

00:50:09.690 --> 00:50:12.940
AUDIENCE: Without nature, can
consciousness still exist?

00:50:12.940 --> 00:50:13.843
MISRA: Yes.

00:50:13.843 --> 00:50:17.787
AUDIENCE: And I'll ask a
simple question and then--

00:50:17.787 --> 00:50:24.470
do you think that what a human
being is capable of knowing,

00:50:24.470 --> 00:50:26.920
ultimately capable
of knowing, is

00:50:26.920 --> 00:50:30.840
replicable in
artificial intelligence?

00:50:30.840 --> 00:50:32.040
MISRA: The answer is yes.

00:50:32.040 --> 00:50:35.580
The answer-- that's exactly
at heart, is interesting.

00:50:35.580 --> 00:50:40.730
That is, the-- so you
can't say artificial.

00:50:40.730 --> 00:50:42.255
You know, I called--

00:50:42.255 --> 00:50:42.880
I think I was--

00:50:42.880 --> 00:50:44.530
I did not use the
phrase, but I will

00:50:44.530 --> 00:50:46.610
call objective intelligence.

00:50:46.610 --> 00:50:48.850
We are operating on two modes.

00:50:48.850 --> 00:50:50.230
Objective
intelligence, something

00:50:50.230 --> 00:50:54.730
with a longer time scale,
which doesn't get refuted.

00:50:54.730 --> 00:50:55.780
I see you.

00:50:55.780 --> 00:50:59.500
I see you exactly the way
I have seen you before.

00:50:59.500 --> 00:51:02.320
So our perception, our reaction,
our interaction between the two

00:51:02.320 --> 00:51:05.830
people, will not change in the
next five days, next 10 days,

00:51:05.830 --> 00:51:10.540
next 10 years, because
we understand each other.

00:51:10.540 --> 00:51:13.390
So that's our cognitive,
reactionary operation

00:51:13.390 --> 00:51:15.970
between two
individuals, two beings.

00:51:15.970 --> 00:51:19.510
Now once that particular
time scale is shortened--

00:51:19.510 --> 00:51:21.290
you go out-- because
I don't know you.

00:51:21.290 --> 00:51:23.980
I go out, I say
yes, I saw that guy.

00:51:23.980 --> 00:51:27.010
So then what happens
is you are operating on

00:51:27.010 --> 00:51:30.640
a lower level, on a
subjective intelligence,

00:51:30.640 --> 00:51:35.080
where as a mutual
convenience, but operating on

00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:37.900
as though that we have
something to deal with.

00:51:37.900 --> 00:51:39.220
We have business.

00:51:39.220 --> 00:51:40.810
We have interest.

00:51:40.810 --> 00:51:46.320
We have togetherness, which is
smaller compared to the larger

00:51:46.320 --> 00:51:49.610
permanence that knowledge
would be all about,

00:51:49.610 --> 00:51:51.420
that truth would be all about.

00:51:51.420 --> 00:51:54.390
And hence why I like the
machine point of view,

00:51:54.390 --> 00:51:56.910
that machines will not change.

00:51:56.910 --> 00:51:59.710
Once we train them on the
objective intelligence,

00:51:59.710 --> 00:52:04.110
whatever we have
found naturally--

00:52:04.110 --> 00:52:07.460
objective intelligence, again,
have their own time scales,

00:52:07.460 --> 00:52:08.790
right?

00:52:08.790 --> 00:52:11.430
You know, Newton's
laws, relativity.

00:52:11.430 --> 00:52:13.620
So things do happen.

00:52:13.620 --> 00:52:15.930
So things are not permanent.

00:52:15.930 --> 00:52:19.920
But we have some
semi-permanence we can build in.

00:52:19.920 --> 00:52:24.060
And hence probably we can create
super smart machines who deal

00:52:24.060 --> 00:52:27.540
with that, who are not really
subjectively cognizing,

00:52:27.540 --> 00:52:32.180
but objectively cognizing,
who cannot really go--

00:52:32.180 --> 00:52:34.250
you know, something
dressed up and so on-- yes,

00:52:34.250 --> 00:52:35.990
this looks good.

00:52:35.990 --> 00:52:36.590
No.

00:52:36.590 --> 00:52:38.870
I know that man.

00:52:38.870 --> 00:52:41.060
I know the nature.

00:52:41.060 --> 00:52:43.270
And I mean, whatever we
can fool-- that's exactly

00:52:43.270 --> 00:52:46.850
Shankara will talk very strongly
that we are subjectively,

00:52:46.850 --> 00:52:49.790
all the time, fooling ourselves.

00:52:49.790 --> 00:52:52.250
So you have to go inside,
strongly concentrate

00:52:52.250 --> 00:52:54.260
who you are, and
then find out you

00:52:54.260 --> 00:52:57.260
have a basic, inside of you,
an objective intelligence,

00:52:57.260 --> 00:53:01.292
and that is independent of you.

00:53:01.292 --> 00:53:01.792
Yes?

00:53:04.720 --> 00:53:06.184
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

00:53:06.184 --> 00:53:08.017
MISRA: Yeah.

00:53:08.017 --> 00:53:11.913
AUDIENCE: You mentioned in
your early part of the lecture

00:53:11.913 --> 00:53:16.296
the avenues of universal
[INAUDIBLE] elements,

00:53:16.296 --> 00:53:19.705
earth, wind, fire, and water.

00:53:19.705 --> 00:53:25.397
Now, in Aristotle's elements,
he describes all these four

00:53:25.397 --> 00:53:29.270
elements, except in the
Indian case, you have sky.

00:53:29.270 --> 00:53:30.000
MISRA: Sky.

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:30.766
AUDIENCE: Space.

00:53:30.766 --> 00:53:31.580
MISRA: Right.

00:53:31.580 --> 00:53:35.210
AUDIENCE: And the concept
of emptiness, space

00:53:35.210 --> 00:53:40.090
probably is instigator
of the concept of zero

00:53:40.090 --> 00:53:43.250
in inventing numerals in India.

00:53:43.250 --> 00:53:45.840
What I wanted to ask you--

00:53:45.840 --> 00:53:48.410
were either the Greeks--

00:53:48.410 --> 00:53:51.370
Greek had interactions with
the Indians at the time.

00:53:51.370 --> 00:53:54.140
Alexander the Great,
when he came to India.

00:53:54.140 --> 00:54:00.162
Or the Indians were [INAUDIBLE]
independently defied out.

00:54:00.162 --> 00:54:02.390
MISRA: I think both
are independently done.

00:54:02.390 --> 00:54:05.210
I think the-- because the
Greeks did not know that

00:54:05.210 --> 00:54:06.770
much of Sanskrit and so on.

00:54:06.770 --> 00:54:09.680
Probably when the Alexander
came to India at that time,

00:54:09.680 --> 00:54:12.440
this was probably already
established, the five elements

00:54:12.440 --> 00:54:13.350
and so on.

00:54:13.350 --> 00:54:17.060
But I don't think he spent
enough time or the interaction

00:54:17.060 --> 00:54:21.140
was enough to really
carry this out to--

00:54:21.140 --> 00:54:22.760
and by the-- also, by the time--

00:54:22.760 --> 00:54:24.460
Aristotle is old by that time.

00:54:24.460 --> 00:54:26.960
So I think his material--

00:54:26.960 --> 00:54:29.750
he doesn't wait for
Alexander come back

00:54:29.750 --> 00:54:32.330
and deliver him material.

00:54:32.330 --> 00:54:34.750
And also, space as a concept--

00:54:37.990 --> 00:54:40.120
this is all hypothetical,
like whether they

00:54:40.120 --> 00:54:42.610
took the five elements and
chopped one and so on because

00:54:42.610 --> 00:54:44.020
of the void, and--

00:54:44.020 --> 00:54:45.560
but I don't think
that's the case.

00:54:45.560 --> 00:54:46.610
I think what--

00:54:46.610 --> 00:54:51.790
I think the visible operations--

00:54:51.790 --> 00:54:55.210
you can make a cosmology
out of the elements,

00:54:55.210 --> 00:54:57.400
Aristotelian elements.

00:54:57.400 --> 00:55:04.510
But to think about
space as an element,

00:55:04.510 --> 00:55:08.910
to sound as a attribute
to that element--

00:55:08.910 --> 00:55:11.040
and human beings
have a speech, have

00:55:11.040 --> 00:55:15.870
the fundamentally different
than other objects

00:55:15.870 --> 00:55:17.500
to make that happen.

00:55:17.500 --> 00:55:19.819
So those are all
metaphysical, which

00:55:19.819 --> 00:55:22.110
probably Indians were somewhat
advanced than the Greeks

00:55:22.110 --> 00:55:23.500
at that time.

00:55:23.500 --> 00:55:24.910
Yeah?

00:55:24.910 --> 00:55:28.670
AUDIENCE: I can [INAUDIBLE]
remark on both this talk

00:55:28.670 --> 00:55:30.440
and the structure of the talks.

00:55:30.440 --> 00:55:31.195
MISRA: Yeah.

00:55:31.195 --> 00:55:32.625
AUDIENCE: I think
we deal here, is

00:55:32.625 --> 00:55:34.430
like two directions of thought.

00:55:34.430 --> 00:55:36.592
One is a traditional
thought with

00:55:36.592 --> 00:55:39.716
[? general ?] understanding
of the world and also ethical

00:55:39.716 --> 00:55:42.096
philosophy that is
called religion.

00:55:42.096 --> 00:55:45.660
And that's the same thing
[INAUDIBLE] understand without

00:55:45.660 --> 00:55:49.630
data, but it's still our--

00:55:49.630 --> 00:55:53.336
more of an ethical attitudes
to things that that's partly,

00:55:53.336 --> 00:55:54.890
what [INAUDIBLE] now.

00:55:54.890 --> 00:55:56.790
And the other thing
is science, that

00:55:56.790 --> 00:56:05.358
is, the [INAUDIBLE] in terms
of motivational structure.

00:56:05.358 --> 00:56:08.850
So it's natural to try
to reconcile the two,

00:56:08.850 --> 00:56:12.355
but things like recapitulating
the ancient ideas

00:56:12.355 --> 00:56:14.762
of cognitive science like
Shankara, Artistotle,

00:56:14.762 --> 00:56:17.730
somehow don't do it to me.

00:56:17.730 --> 00:56:19.550
MISRA: Don't do what?

00:56:19.550 --> 00:56:23.452
AUDIENCE: They-- it's primitive
science, is my opinion.

00:56:23.452 --> 00:56:25.174
It's primitive
cognitive science there,

00:56:25.174 --> 00:56:27.880
but, of course, it doesn't
appeal to my ethics.

00:56:27.880 --> 00:56:30.340
And maybe we can
also sometimes hear

00:56:30.340 --> 00:56:33.490
opinions of people who are
not trying to reconcile

00:56:33.490 --> 00:56:35.226
those things, but think that--

00:56:35.226 --> 00:56:37.560
MISRA: It's primitive because
it's done at old time,

00:56:37.560 --> 00:56:39.631
or primitive because
the ideas are--

00:56:39.631 --> 00:56:41.630
because it's thousand
years old, it's primitive,

00:56:41.630 --> 00:56:43.200
or because you think
that's mundane,

00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:44.890
and should not discuss?

00:56:44.890 --> 00:56:47.752
AUDIENCE: Neuroscience, how
the brain is really designed--

00:56:47.752 --> 00:56:49.720
some of these
things are out of--

00:56:49.720 --> 00:56:52.120
MISRA: Because neuroscience
doesn't answer this.

00:56:52.120 --> 00:56:54.040
We go back to consciousness.

00:56:54.040 --> 00:56:56.710
See, consciousness
is a particular--

00:56:56.710 --> 00:56:59.250
that's exactly-- I went to
the brain mapping project.

00:56:59.250 --> 00:57:01.450
The consciousness,
if we can find

00:57:01.450 --> 00:57:04.300
in your brain what
cells are there

00:57:04.300 --> 00:57:07.730
which makes you conscious.

00:57:07.730 --> 00:57:11.750
It's not a function of how
you hear or how you see

00:57:11.750 --> 00:57:13.510
or how you sense.

00:57:13.510 --> 00:57:17.500
It's a function of what
makes you conscious.

00:57:17.500 --> 00:57:19.635
Our instruments at
the present time,

00:57:19.635 --> 00:57:21.010
our thoughts at
the present time,

00:57:21.010 --> 00:57:23.470
have failed to
even understand how

00:57:23.470 --> 00:57:26.500
we synthesize, how
the mind functions,

00:57:26.500 --> 00:57:28.530
even from sensory perception.

00:57:28.530 --> 00:57:31.730
What you are receiving is
only some kind of sketches.

00:57:31.730 --> 00:57:34.040
We're receiving
only small signals.

00:57:34.040 --> 00:57:37.060
Remember I said in the beginning
that we have this very, very

00:57:37.060 --> 00:57:39.460
sketchy signals that are coming
from different directions

00:57:39.460 --> 00:57:40.360
to you.

00:57:40.360 --> 00:57:43.630
You are processing them
to create an image.

00:57:43.630 --> 00:57:46.480
That processing, how it is
done, which part of the brain

00:57:46.480 --> 00:57:48.850
does that, we don't know.

00:57:48.850 --> 00:57:50.650
That's the reason why
we are going to make

00:57:50.650 --> 00:57:53.140
these five-micron brain map.

00:57:53.140 --> 00:57:56.620
Hopefully, we can navigate
and see where it is happening.

00:57:56.620 --> 00:57:59.160
Not that I can
guarantee we can see it,

00:57:59.160 --> 00:58:00.160
but that's the question.

00:58:00.160 --> 00:58:02.710
The question is, we
have all these neurons,

00:58:02.710 --> 00:58:06.520
we know how these neurons
are activating themselves,

00:58:06.520 --> 00:58:11.380
we know how they are reacting
to different sensory operations,

00:58:11.380 --> 00:58:14.610
but we don't know how
they're synthesizing,

00:58:14.610 --> 00:58:17.100
if they're synthesizing,
what time scale

00:58:17.100 --> 00:58:18.840
they're synthesizing.

00:58:18.840 --> 00:58:21.300
And then the question is,
if they're synthesizing,

00:58:21.300 --> 00:58:27.440
what happens to the perception
of it, the knowledge of it?

00:58:27.440 --> 00:58:29.670
What the consciousness--
you had a good question.

00:58:29.670 --> 00:58:33.630
Consciousness could be some
kind of a genetic cell.

00:58:33.630 --> 00:58:35.700
That's what I think.

00:58:35.700 --> 00:58:39.390
It could be a very minute cell
which probably operates in all

00:58:39.390 --> 00:58:42.090
of us in different degrees.

00:58:42.090 --> 00:58:46.930
And probably, in some process,
we get activated to it.

00:58:46.930 --> 00:58:48.310
Could be.

00:58:48.310 --> 00:58:51.280
But you can't deny
the fact that you

00:58:51.280 --> 00:58:54.190
are not conscious all the time.

00:58:54.190 --> 00:58:57.150
You can't deny the fact that
sometimes you're conscious,

00:58:57.150 --> 00:58:58.710
sometimes not conscious.

00:58:58.710 --> 00:59:00.250
And your brain doesn't say that.

00:59:00.250 --> 00:59:03.420
But the same brain, the
same memory, the same mind,

00:59:03.420 --> 00:59:08.960
the same intellect, same body,
same blood, goes unconscious.

00:59:08.960 --> 00:59:11.180
That's the question.

00:59:11.180 --> 00:59:13.330
It happens in children more.

00:59:13.330 --> 00:59:14.460
Yes?

00:59:14.460 --> 00:59:15.960
FOERST: No, please,
please go ahead.

00:59:15.960 --> 00:59:18.376
I just would like to finish
to answer his second question.

00:59:18.376 --> 00:59:19.800
MISRA: Yeah, another question?

00:59:19.800 --> 00:59:20.890
FOERST: His second--

00:59:20.890 --> 00:59:23.060
No, his second question was--

00:59:23.060 --> 00:59:24.920
to the structure of
the lecture series,

00:59:24.920 --> 00:59:28.050
I don't try to reconcile
religion and science.

00:59:28.050 --> 00:59:30.990
I try to present a variety
of different scientists

00:59:30.990 --> 00:59:33.120
and their ways to
deal with these two.

00:59:33.120 --> 00:59:36.300
So today Professor Misra
tries to reconcile them.

00:59:36.300 --> 00:59:38.920
We had other people who
try to keep them apart.

00:59:38.920 --> 00:59:42.000
We have other people who try to
keep them kind of in a balance,

00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:42.740
but still--

00:59:42.740 --> 00:59:46.600
I've tried to present a variety
of people with different ways.

00:59:46.600 --> 00:59:50.361
So it's not an overall objective
goal to bring the two together.

00:59:50.361 --> 00:59:52.360
I don't know-- it's
probably your first lecture,

00:59:52.360 --> 00:59:53.190
otherwise you--

00:59:53.190 --> 00:59:56.137
AUDIENCE: No, I've been
here for multiple talks.

00:59:56.137 --> 00:59:59.710
But I would like to hear
two more people, one

00:59:59.710 --> 01:00:02.906
who thinks that religion is it
and science doesn't do anything

01:00:02.906 --> 01:00:05.774
and its view of the
world is hogwash,

01:00:05.774 --> 01:00:07.845
and the other person
who would think

01:00:07.845 --> 01:00:10.076
the same thing about religion.

01:00:10.076 --> 01:00:12.720
Not people who have both
things and try and--

01:00:12.720 --> 01:00:15.090
FOERST: Well, you know, I
tried to invite those people.

01:00:15.090 --> 01:00:17.940
But people, if you think
that science is bogus,

01:00:17.940 --> 01:00:20.654
are not scientists, and
therefore they wouldn't--

01:00:20.654 --> 01:00:23.070
I cannot present them here as
scientists doing that stuff.

01:00:23.070 --> 01:00:24.319
And people who hate religion--

01:00:24.319 --> 01:00:27.670
I invited several people,
and they all denied to come.

01:00:27.670 --> 01:00:31.000
So in that sense, it's--

01:00:31.000 --> 01:00:33.390
MISRA: No, if you asked me
what my personal opinion--

01:00:33.390 --> 01:00:35.642
religion is bogus.

01:00:35.642 --> 01:00:36.350
FOERST: Oh, good.

01:00:36.350 --> 01:00:37.850
MISRA: I didn't say
religion at all.

01:00:37.850 --> 01:00:40.660
Did I use the word
religion at all?

01:00:40.660 --> 01:00:42.060
There's no religion.

01:00:42.060 --> 01:00:44.700
It's a question ignorance.

01:00:44.700 --> 01:00:46.980
Ignorance to the
point that you use

01:00:46.980 --> 01:00:49.864
the perception, and perception
for a short time scale.

01:00:49.864 --> 01:00:51.030
I don't know-- what's your--

01:00:51.030 --> 01:00:53.610
you are a physicist,
chemist, computer scientist?

01:00:53.610 --> 01:00:54.210
Yeah.

01:00:54.210 --> 01:00:55.330
So time scale.

01:00:55.330 --> 01:00:57.450
We're talking about cosmology.

01:00:57.450 --> 01:01:00.690
We're talking about how
the universe begins.

01:01:00.690 --> 01:01:04.290
How does the universe
sustain itself?

01:01:04.290 --> 01:01:09.960
Do the laws that we think are
true here are true elsewhere?

01:01:09.960 --> 01:01:14.010
Are they true in you and in me?

01:01:14.010 --> 01:01:16.140
If not, why not?

01:01:16.140 --> 01:01:19.500
What we are talking consciously,
from our small experiment--

01:01:19.500 --> 01:01:22.330
which you can do yourself--

01:01:22.330 --> 01:01:24.840
that you and your friend,
seeing the same object,

01:01:24.840 --> 01:01:27.390
may not have the
same perception.

01:01:27.390 --> 01:01:29.265
That's where the cognitive
weakness comes in.

01:01:32.520 --> 01:01:36.034
If the same-- you can make
experiments with color.

01:01:36.034 --> 01:01:37.700
You can make experiments
from the stars.

01:01:37.700 --> 01:01:39.560
You can make
experiments on the--

01:01:39.560 --> 01:01:42.419
you know, why we
thought astrology

01:01:42.419 --> 01:01:44.210
was an important
parameter for a long time,

01:01:44.210 --> 01:01:46.270
why people still think.

01:01:46.270 --> 01:01:48.110
This sky looks 2D.

01:01:48.110 --> 01:01:50.689
Sky looks like it's spherical.

01:01:50.689 --> 01:01:51.855
That's a cognitive weakness.

01:01:54.910 --> 01:01:58.450
The sky, which expands
so much behind--

01:01:58.450 --> 01:02:00.400
looking to you, it's a sphere.

01:02:00.400 --> 01:02:02.910
Stars hanging in this
particular sphere

01:02:02.910 --> 01:02:06.270
is our cognitive weakness.

01:02:06.270 --> 01:02:07.950
Ignorance.

01:02:07.950 --> 01:02:09.750
And we stayed with
it for a long time.

01:02:09.750 --> 01:02:11.580
We still probably--
you know, whatever

01:02:11.580 --> 01:02:14.390
we know now is still weak.

01:02:14.390 --> 01:02:16.030
So that is what
you would inquire,

01:02:16.030 --> 01:02:18.430
that is there truth
means how long

01:02:18.430 --> 01:02:22.300
in knowledge, what timescale
the knowledge may have,

01:02:22.300 --> 01:02:24.820
and further, we
can always receive

01:02:24.820 --> 01:02:29.020
full cognitive conscious
feedback from our observation,

01:02:29.020 --> 01:02:30.490
from our senses.

01:02:30.490 --> 01:02:31.986
What he's saying--
again, I don't

01:02:31.986 --> 01:02:34.110
know whether it is right
or wrong to talk Shankara.

01:02:34.110 --> 01:02:36.100
I think it's a pleasure
to talk Shankara and so

01:02:36.100 --> 01:02:37.510
on, because I admire him.

01:02:37.510 --> 01:02:40.750
But what he says is that
probably you will never

01:02:40.750 --> 01:02:42.750
have access to full truth.

01:02:42.750 --> 01:02:44.500
Then he of course
becomes godly and so on,

01:02:44.500 --> 01:02:45.940
which you can question.

01:02:45.940 --> 01:02:47.740
I didn't show his--

01:02:47.740 --> 01:02:52.300
I made a little picture for
him, who did not come out well.

01:02:52.300 --> 01:02:53.931
But you know, it
kind of inkjet--

01:02:53.931 --> 01:02:56.430
I think it kind of-- you will
kind of snark at this and say,

01:02:56.430 --> 01:02:59.590
wow, he shows a religious
person's picture

01:02:59.590 --> 01:03:00.530
here and so on.

01:03:00.530 --> 01:03:01.675
But I will show you anyway.

01:03:04.900 --> 01:03:06.870
It's kind of a typical--

01:03:06.870 --> 01:03:09.910
it's some kind of artist
projection of the man,

01:03:09.910 --> 01:03:10.480
all right?

01:03:10.480 --> 01:03:13.405
But the point is why this man
thinks about this, whether it's

01:03:13.405 --> 01:03:16.420
a scientist, a religious
scholar, philosopher,

01:03:16.420 --> 01:03:17.800
or has a very high IQ.

01:03:17.800 --> 01:03:18.820
I don't know.

01:03:18.820 --> 01:03:26.890
But what kind of makes me wonder
that he did think about this

01:03:26.890 --> 01:03:31.150
particular knowledge and
ignorance in the scientific

01:03:31.150 --> 01:03:35.980
way, that [INAUDIBLE] talks
about in 1923, the same things,

01:03:35.980 --> 01:03:38.920
not with that particular
detail, but with experimental--

01:03:38.920 --> 01:03:41.340
I don't think he
did an experiment.

01:03:41.340 --> 01:03:43.050
It's pure intuition.

01:03:43.050 --> 01:03:44.020
okay, what else?

01:03:44.020 --> 01:03:44.520
Yes?

01:03:44.520 --> 01:03:46.444
AUDIENCE: Yes, according
to your lecture,

01:03:46.444 --> 01:03:51.254
would it be correct for me
to assume that a machine can

01:03:51.254 --> 01:03:57.660
be intelligent, but a machine
can never be knowledgeable?

01:03:57.660 --> 01:03:59.580
MISRA: Machine is
conditioned to be

01:03:59.580 --> 01:04:02.610
knowledgeable to the point
that to inject knowledge to it.

01:04:02.610 --> 01:04:05.496
AUDIENCE: Right, but that makes
it illusional, because there's

01:04:05.496 --> 01:04:08.310
always a knowledge beyond that.

01:04:08.310 --> 01:04:11.770
So a machine will always
be only delusional,

01:04:11.770 --> 01:04:16.080
only be intelligent, but
never fully knowledgeable.

01:04:16.080 --> 01:04:17.290
MISRA: Like all we are.

01:04:17.290 --> 01:04:21.390
AUDIENCE: So that [INAUDIBLE]
with the Hindu religion.

01:04:21.390 --> 01:04:22.442
The Hindus--

01:04:22.442 --> 01:04:23.400
MISRA: That is correct.

01:04:23.400 --> 01:04:24.012
Yeah.

01:04:24.012 --> 01:04:26.220
Yeah, what-- it's not a
Hindu religion from Shankara.

01:04:26.220 --> 01:04:29.220
I think the-- suppose you ask
a Hindu religious person some,

01:04:29.220 --> 01:04:30.314
he will say he knows it.

01:04:30.314 --> 01:04:31.230
AUDIENCE: He knows it.

01:04:31.230 --> 01:04:32.310
MISRA: He knows it.

01:04:32.310 --> 01:04:34.010
Do a prayer or do
something, something,

01:04:34.010 --> 01:04:36.020
you know what to
say the truth is.

01:04:36.020 --> 01:04:38.820
But what he kind
of, [INAUDIBLE] says

01:04:38.820 --> 01:04:43.140
that what you say the
truth has presented to you,

01:04:43.140 --> 01:04:47.600
without having a full
dose of consciousness,

01:04:47.600 --> 01:04:48.549
is only perception.

01:04:48.549 --> 01:04:49.840
AUDIENCE: It's only a delusion.

01:04:49.840 --> 01:04:52.010
MISRA: You take it
with a pinch of salt.

01:04:52.010 --> 01:04:55.231
You take it with a
lot of apprehension.

01:04:55.231 --> 01:04:55.730
And then--

01:04:55.730 --> 01:04:57.604
AUDIENCE: It's the
beginning but not the end.

01:04:57.604 --> 01:04:58.271
MISRA: Right.

01:04:58.271 --> 01:04:58.770
Yes.

01:04:58.770 --> 01:05:00.677
AUDIENCE: The end
is when we're dead.

01:05:00.677 --> 01:05:02.510
MISRA: I don't know
whether you would really

01:05:02.510 --> 01:05:03.800
see the consciousness.

01:05:03.800 --> 01:05:04.850
I think-- I don't know.

01:05:04.850 --> 01:05:06.080
I think that to be--

01:05:06.080 --> 01:05:09.200
they do like in the
[INAUDIBLE] for that gentleman.

01:05:09.200 --> 01:05:12.530
[INAUDIBLE] that doing
the yoga as a technique

01:05:12.530 --> 01:05:14.070
to determine consciousness.

01:05:14.070 --> 01:05:16.850
They're trying to do experiments
to see whether we can really

01:05:16.850 --> 01:05:20.900
see, like when the person is
kind of concentrating strongly,

01:05:20.900 --> 01:05:24.710
whether we can measure
the brain function.

01:05:24.710 --> 01:05:25.962
So that results will come out.

01:05:25.962 --> 01:05:27.170
They're not come out with it.

01:05:27.170 --> 01:05:32.940
I think last week there's
some kind of epileptic--

01:05:32.940 --> 01:05:36.200
you know, epilepsy-- those
kind of results came out

01:05:36.200 --> 01:05:38.590
in neuroscience-- in the
conference last week.

01:05:38.590 --> 01:05:40.670
But some more things
will come in next--

01:05:40.670 --> 01:05:44.000
they said this is the
year of the brain, right?

01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:46.359
Decade of the brain.

01:05:46.359 --> 01:05:47.150
Any other question?

01:05:47.150 --> 01:05:48.450
Yes?

01:05:48.450 --> 01:05:49.450
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE].

01:05:49.450 --> 01:05:52.130
MISRA: Oh, okay.

01:05:52.130 --> 01:05:54.110
AUDIENCE: But go to the
other slide, please.

01:05:54.110 --> 01:05:55.595
MISRA: Okay.

01:05:55.595 --> 01:05:58.940
AUDIENCE: Gentleman on the
left has a [INAUDIBLE]..

01:05:58.940 --> 01:06:04.278
She asks you about
a [INAUDIBLE] genes.

01:06:04.278 --> 01:06:10.596
And the organizer
asked about [INAUDIBLE]

01:06:10.596 --> 01:06:13.755
and your own last
sentence there says

01:06:13.755 --> 01:06:16.914
knowledge of the [INAUDIBLE]
is the only truth.

01:06:16.914 --> 01:06:19.360
Shankara only are your truth.

01:06:19.360 --> 01:06:24.300
And also, therefore,
copying from ancient texts

01:06:24.300 --> 01:06:28.340
wherein this pursuit of this
knowledge at this stage--

01:06:28.340 --> 01:06:30.840
lore, truth,
knowledge, and love.

01:06:30.840 --> 01:06:32.830
They are all mushed together.

01:06:32.830 --> 01:06:38.220
It means a dichotomy
[INAUDIBLE]..

01:06:38.220 --> 01:06:41.650
My question is, in this
part-- you wil tell me

01:06:41.650 --> 01:06:47.530
what you got also, in this
part of attaining that state,

01:06:47.530 --> 01:06:51.853
the text is neither
the full [INAUDIBLE]..

01:06:54.690 --> 01:06:57.577
Can those bodies-- You
know them, of course.

01:06:57.577 --> 01:06:58.410
MISRA: I know, but--

01:06:58.410 --> 01:07:01.525
AUDIENCE: Nobody's
ever been [INAUDIBLE]..

01:07:01.525 --> 01:07:03.400
MISRA: I don't think we
should get into that,

01:07:03.400 --> 01:07:06.270
I don't think the cognition,
like what do you feel--

01:07:06.270 --> 01:07:10.200
like what happens when you go
to the objective intelligence?

01:07:10.200 --> 01:07:14.370
Like human beings know.

01:07:14.370 --> 01:07:16.140
I think that, again, know--

01:07:16.140 --> 01:07:17.880
see, this has been
done by children.

01:07:17.880 --> 01:07:20.680
[INAUDIBLE]

01:07:20.680 --> 01:07:22.670
Have bunch of kids,
10 kids, all right?

01:07:22.670 --> 01:07:26.880
You quiz them, how much
they know, what they know.

01:07:26.880 --> 01:07:30.825
Then you can find out
where the loopholes are.

01:07:30.825 --> 01:07:33.060
For the adults, it's
difficult to do,

01:07:33.060 --> 01:07:35.850
because adults have so
much different knowledge.

01:07:35.850 --> 01:07:37.820
And an experiment
to say that, look,

01:07:37.820 --> 01:07:40.380
where the ignorance level is
and how high the ignorance

01:07:40.380 --> 01:07:42.840
level is, what we do
is we do the testing.

01:07:42.840 --> 01:07:44.460
We do the exams and so on.

01:07:44.460 --> 01:07:45.180
And people flunk.

01:07:45.180 --> 01:07:46.170
People move.

01:07:46.170 --> 01:07:47.580
Things happen like that.

01:07:47.580 --> 01:07:53.670
But that is not cognitive test,
that yes, I know my friend.

01:07:53.670 --> 01:07:56.080
I know my father.

01:07:56.080 --> 01:07:58.710
I think mother and son,
probably a little different,

01:07:58.710 --> 01:08:00.990
because mothers know their
sons, but sons do not

01:08:00.990 --> 01:08:03.600
know the-- for example, I tell
you one particular experience

01:08:03.600 --> 01:08:05.580
on my part.

01:08:05.580 --> 01:08:07.330
I look somewhat
different from my family.

01:08:07.330 --> 01:08:08.340
I don't know why.

01:08:08.340 --> 01:08:11.370
So we had a person we were
working for in our home,

01:08:11.370 --> 01:08:14.637
and she kind of made me
feel that-- and my mom

01:08:14.637 --> 01:08:15.470
was a little strict.

01:08:15.470 --> 01:08:17.229
She was a very strong
disciplinarian.

01:08:17.229 --> 01:08:19.634
So she will kind of always
yell that if I don't come home

01:08:19.634 --> 01:08:21.050
at a particular
time or something.

01:08:21.050 --> 01:08:22.830
So this woman, for
whatever reason,

01:08:22.830 --> 01:08:25.470
she will tell me that,
look, you are not her son.

01:08:25.470 --> 01:08:27.870
[LAUGHTER]

01:08:27.870 --> 01:08:30.510
And I mean, I was, like, 11,
12 years old or something.

01:08:30.510 --> 01:08:32.680
I said, wow.

01:08:32.680 --> 01:08:34.710
How do I deal with
this, you know?

01:08:34.710 --> 01:08:36.420
How do I deal with this?

01:08:36.420 --> 01:08:37.890
What is this?

01:08:37.890 --> 01:08:38.850
So I talked to her--

01:08:38.850 --> 01:08:41.700
I had-- you know, my
father is a liberal person.

01:08:41.700 --> 01:08:42.510
So we had, like--

01:08:42.510 --> 01:08:44.856
I called a conference.

01:08:44.856 --> 01:08:45.689
My father was there.

01:08:45.689 --> 01:08:46.855
Mom was there in this thing.

01:08:46.855 --> 01:08:47.370
I sat down.

01:08:47.370 --> 01:08:49.319
I said, look, I have something
important to ask, and so on.

01:08:49.319 --> 01:08:51.069
And then they said--
they're sitting here.

01:08:51.069 --> 01:08:52.029
I'm sitting here.

01:08:52.029 --> 01:08:53.370
So I told them.

01:08:53.370 --> 01:08:55.140
It was 1959.

01:08:55.140 --> 01:08:58.818
I asked them-- I asked my dad,
but how do I know I'm your son?

01:08:58.818 --> 01:09:00.690
[LAUGHTER]

01:09:01.630 --> 01:09:04.069
How do you know you
are your father's son?

01:09:04.069 --> 01:09:06.140
You can do a DNA test now.

01:09:06.140 --> 01:09:08.840
Shankara didn't know that.

01:09:08.840 --> 01:09:11.689
My point is these
are cognitive issues,

01:09:11.689 --> 01:09:14.810
issues that you,
through your perception,

01:09:14.810 --> 01:09:18.050
through your senses, you're
receiving information

01:09:18.050 --> 01:09:22.229
from the other object to
create an association.

01:09:22.229 --> 01:09:26.370
That association, how scientific
it is, how truthful it is,

01:09:26.370 --> 01:09:29.149
how objective it
is, is up to you.

01:09:29.149 --> 01:09:32.160
What this says-- it
can become objective

01:09:32.160 --> 01:09:34.806
if you are totally conscious.

01:09:34.806 --> 01:09:40.470
Unfortunately, we are not
all the time fully conscious.

01:09:40.470 --> 01:09:41.810
Is there a way to be conscious?

01:09:41.810 --> 01:09:43.049
We do not know.

01:09:43.049 --> 01:09:44.714
And religion takes over there.

01:09:44.714 --> 01:09:46.380
FOERST: I'm sorry,
we have to interrupt.

01:09:46.380 --> 01:09:46.880
MISRA: okay.

01:09:46.880 --> 01:09:47.410
Very good.

01:09:47.410 --> 01:09:47.880
Thank you again.

01:09:47.880 --> 01:09:49.421
FOERST: Thank you
so much for coming.

01:09:49.421 --> 01:09:52.430
[APPLAUSE]

